# Smith - A named assembly and print pack

```elixir
Mix.install([{:smith, "~> 0.1.0"}, {:kino, "~> 0.19.0"}])
```

## Define a reusable part

Use ordinary functions for features and parameters. Both instances below reuse the
same recipe, which Smith evaluates once within this assembly evaluation.

```elixir
defmodule NotebookParts do
  def foot(width, depth, height) do
    Smith.box(width, depth, height)
    |> Smith.fillet(edges: {:parallel, :z}, count: 4, radius: 1)
    |> Smith.hole(on: :top, diameter: 5, through: :all)
  end
end
foot = NotebookParts.foot(12, 16, 8)
{:ok, preview} = Smith.Kino.render(foot, label: "1 · Reusable foot")
preview
```

## Place two instances

Installed geometry and printable orientation are independent. References are
available for inspection but excluded from manufactured geometry and print packs.

```elixir
alias Smith.Assembly
pair =
  Assembly.new(:support)
  |> Assembly.part(:left, foot, position: {-20, 0, 0}, print: [on_bed: true])
  |> Assembly.part(:right, foot, position: {20, 0, 0}, print: [on_bed: true])
  |> Assembly.reference(:device, Smith.box(28, 16, 6), position: {-8, 0, 8})
{:ok, result} = Smith.evaluate(pair)
{:ok, preview} = Smith.Kino.render(result, label: "2 · Installed feet")
preview
```

## Inspect a reference

```elixir
{:ok, device} = Assembly.fetch(result, :device)
{:ok, preview} = Smith.Kino.render(device, label: "Reference · Device")
preview
```

## Export the complete assembly

Each manufactured part gets verified STL and 3MF files. The bundle also includes
installed STEP geometry, a separate reference STEP, and a ZIP of printable parts.

```elixir
{:ok, solids} = OCEx.solids(result.shape)
2 = length(solids)
{:ok, files} = Smith.export(result, "output/livebook", name: "support")
files
```
